 "seesTitle": "What Santuari de Sant Salvador sees",
 "seesHTML": "Cura's east-coast twin, and by the numbers its equal or better: from the 472 m Crist Rei knoll the whole island lies between you and the sun, and the Tramuntana silhouette under the totality sun is 65 km away \u2014 a pencil line of ~0.15\u00b0, leaving \u22482.0\u00b0 of clear sky. The umbra sweep is the grandest of any spot: the shadow crosses the Tramuntana, races the width of Es Pla toward you, and climbs your hill. The closing image is unique \u2014 the crescent sets at \u224820:45 behind the Randa massif, the sister sanctuary's own hill.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from Santuari de Sant Salvador: terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:45.",
 "recoTitle": "Around Santuari de Sant Salvador",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The west terraces and the Crist Rei knoll</b> \u2014 proper summit road, real parking, and more west-facing room than Cura; still, arrive well before 19:30.</li><li><b>The monastery bar/guesthouse</b> \u2014 the only green spot with services on site.</li><li><b>Coming from the east coast</b> \u2014 this beats driving across the island; Cala d'Or and Porto Cristo below are risky/blocked.</li>",
 "verdictText": "Totality with 2.0\u00b0 to spare \u2014 terrain takes the crescent at \u224820:45"
